{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["Was that why he called his name Jacob — in astonishment: was it so that, because he was called Jacob at birth since his hand was grasping the heel, and I am found to be the firstborn — that he should take double from me?! And it is plain that if he was younger he should have taken less than me, yet he takes double. And likewise: הכי אחי אתה — is it enough for you to take a great reward, and you have served me for nothing?! — in astonishment. And likewise in Bava Batra we learned in the chapter: one who dies when the assets are plentiful — the sons inherit and the daughters are fed. If the assets are meager — the daughters are fed and the sons must beg at the doors. Admon says: is it because I am a male and my claim is stronger when the assets are plentiful, that my claim is weaker when the assets are meager?! — in astonishment."], :book :genesis, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 27, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:45:30.054117865Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}